---
description: Domain rules for contacts, drafts, send, and Apollo import
alwaysApply: true
---

# Outreach invariants

- `Contact.email` is unique. Apollo locked rows use `email_not_unlocked+<apolloId>@apollo.local`. Never collapse those onto a shared email.
- Apollo import dedupes by `apolloPersonId`, not email. Companies use deterministic `company-<slug>` ids.
- Draft machine: `PENDING_REVIEW` → `APPROVED` → `SENT`. `POST /api/send` must send only `APPROVED` drafts.
- Keep send pacing (delay + daily cap from `AppSettings`, defaults 2s / 100). Do not bulk-fire Resend.
- Generate pacing stays ~2100ms per contact. On Groq quota errors, skip remaining contacts.
- Webhooks: bounce → `BOUNCED`, complaint → `UNSUBSCRIBED`. Keep signature checks.
- Email `ContactStatus` helpers in `contacts-url.ts` must match `prisma/schema.prisma`. LinkedIn uses `NEW` / `OUTREACHED` in `linkedin-status.ts` (legacy `CONTACTED` maps to `OUTREACHED`).
- There is no auth; treat every API as admin. Do not expand `/api/debug`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
await sendEmail({ to: draft.contact.email, ... }); // ignores APPROVED + pacing

// ✅ GOOD
where: { id: { in: draftIds }, status: "APPROVED" }
```
